{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1508716-who-can-see-a-wraith","id":1508716,"title":"Who can see a wraith","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-18T00:51:03-07:00","id":1508716,"title":"Who can see a wraith","content":"At one time, I recall a person who was a fetter could see a wraith, a supernatural person who was a fetter could do it automatically as I recall.<br /> <br /> But who can see a wraith without the use of gifts, spheres, disciplines, arcanoi, etc?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23984-thkaal","name":"Thkaal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T01:17:27-07:00","id":1508719,"title":"","content":"I could be forgetting something, but if &quot;etc.&quot; includes Merits? I think only Projector Orpheus agents have the innate ability to see wraiths rather than having to have a purchasable power/Merit to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T03:19:25-07:00","id":1508729,"title":"","content":"I think even projectors can only see wraiths when they're actually projecting in the Underworld themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T03:38:29-07:00","id":1508731,"title":"","content":"The Dead Eye's innate ability isn't as specific as it could be about if you actually need to be projecting to benefit from it (some of the others are more explicit about this). Though there's no reason why they have to be projected into the Underworld even if they have to be projected... they could still be on this side of things even if incorporeal or manifested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T05:25:29-07:00","id":1508737,"title":"","content":"Depends if we're talking original Orpheus or Wr20. In the latter case there is just the Skinlands and the Underworld, no incorporeal place in between.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T08:58:44-07:00","id":1508755,"title":"","content":"I don't remember the wording of Dead-Eyes in Orpheus, but whether skimmers have it when they are projecting is a recurring question. Certainly the events of Crusade of Ashes are harder to explain if Skimmers and Sleepers could see ghosts coming, but the same could be said for any projecting sleepers or ghosts on staff. <br /> <br /> In Wr20 it is an activatable power that projectors can use &quot;in the meat.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T11:47:17-07:00","id":1508767,"title":"","content":"Sluagh can see wraiths with a Perception+Kenning roll (and speak to them with a point of Glamour) as part of their Sharpened Senses Birthright.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T17:40:10-07:00","id":1508796,"title":"","content":"Apparently certain Malkavians are able to see (or at least sense) the Restless Dead, but this is apparently highly dependent on the Malkavian's specific Derangement and if the idea of the Restless Dead fit within such a thing. For example, there's an EMT template in the revised Malkavian Clanbook who has the derangement Sanguinary Animism, where she believes herself to be haunted by the souls of anyone she's fed upon (especially if the feeding was fatal). In such a case, if someone she fed from became a wraith, then they'd likely be visible to her.<br /> Necropolis: Atlanta's Malkavian Prince was a Civil War veteran whose Derangement was, IIRC, a nigh-total lack of fear of dying. Admittedly, this wasn't a particularly great Derangement, but because of this apparently could see the Restless Dead. <br /> It's the sort of thing that a Storyteller would have to decide on a case by case basis. If a character's Derangement was, say, the delusion that they are dead and in Purgatory, I might allow it, at least from time to time. But if it's something like self-injury syndrome or an obsession with insects, then probably not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T18:55:55-07:00","id":1508805,"title":"","content":"Lots of ordinary people can potentially see Wraiths. This would be a low number overall relative to all of Humanity, but there are lots of potential scenarios.<br /> <br /> Almost anyone can get vague impressions of Wraiths if they are extremely tired, drunk, injured, or otherwise not themselves / out of their mind. They may not realize what they sense is a Wraith, but they can sense something.<br /> <br /> Anyone considered to be an &quot;Innocent&quot; can see a Wraith. This could include small children, certain people who are mad, the very pious, very sheltered peopl, and others.<br /> <br /> Animals often detect Wraiths - the stereotypical pet dog that barks at &quot;nothing&quot;.<br /> <br /> People who are &quot;sensitive&quot;, though this tends to be the same people who count as Mediums and thus have actual Merits, Flaws, or Numina of some kind.<br /> <br /> People who have the Awareness Ability can probably detect Wraiths in some capacity provided they roll to do so.<br /> <br /> I would do the same for people who achieve the Periphery and become spiritually aware - certain situations (not all) might warrant them witnessing a Wraith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T20:30:14-07:00","id":1508818,"title":"","content":"You know, I could swear there was a FAQ somewhere that answered this question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T01:07:05-07:00","id":1508862,"title":"","content":"I know there is a small section that addresses this near the back of the 2e corebook. It's not all in the same spot, but it's there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}